WEBVTT

NOTE English captions for https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rb2EkzjgO98, from YouTube, repeats removed.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Assalamualaikum, warahmatullah wabarakatuh.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.840
I want to thank you for joining me for this short series in this blessed month

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.200
of Ramadan.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.560
Inshallah ta'ala, this month is about spiritual elevation.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.600
It's about deeper understanding

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:19.240
of our relationship with Allah subhana wa ta'ala and with the Rasul sallallahu alaihi wa sallam.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:25.440
A deep part of Ramadan is gaining deeper insight into how Allah subhana wa ta'ala blesses

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.720
us, how we are to get close to Allah subhana wa ta'ala, and deeper understanding of

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.680
who we are as people and who we should aspire to be as believers.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.240
Inshallah, over these next few videos, I'm going to be taking you through a well-known collection

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:47.600
of short, beautiful phrases that have been crafted and written by none other than Ibn Ata'illah

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.520
al-Iskandari.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:56.120
This book is known as al-Hikam, which just means these aphorisms or these short sayings that

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:00.000
are filled with wisdom and a lot for us to think about.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.040
The words are short, but the meanings are deep.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:09.320
And inshallah, I thank you for joining me for these gems of reflection and depth uh

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.720
through the insight of Ibn Ata'illah al-Iskandari.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:18.000
So, with that said, inshallah, we're going to move into our first one for today, inshallah

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.600
ta'ala.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.000
Ibn Ata'illah, he says,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:30.080
Rubbama waradat al-dhuluma alaik li yu'arrifaka qadra manna bihi alaik.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.000
The Imam, he says

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.760
that sometimes

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.360
darkness will come over our heart.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.240
May- maybe it's a sin that we fall into.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.600
Uh maybe it's a emotional state that we're feeling.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.600
Um any type of darkness will come over our hearts.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.160
And we struggle with wondering why we are experiencing that.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:56.200
We struggle to wonder and understand what is the wisdom behind it, right?

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.280
Um there's a hadith that is quite beautiful.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.600
In which the Rasul alayhi salaat wa salaam, he said that the believer's affair is quite

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.080
unique.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:11.600
If hardship comes, the believer is patient, and that is good.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:16.320
And if ease comes, the believer is grateful, and that is also good.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:21.240
What the Prophet alayhi salaat wa salaam was teaching us in this Hadith is that

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.160
it's all good, as we used to say.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:28.880
It's all good. Meaning whatever we're going through, there is something there for us to notice.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.640
Something for us to learn.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.080
Some way for us to grow.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:40.640
And so, in this aphorism, in this Hikam, the Imam, he says, that

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.520
sometimes darkness will come over your heart.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.600
It comes in different ways.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:52.840
But why? He says one of the reasons is li yu'arrifaka qadra ma manna bihi alayk.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:58.160
So that he can make you recognize, so that he can make you see

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.440
the value of the blessings that he has given you before.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:05.040
Now, there's a few ways to look at this.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:10.320
There's a saying, you know, like faqidu shay, like a person that doesn't know one realizes

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.840
the blessing of something until it is taken away, until it is gone.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.560
What the Imam is saying here is sometimes

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.600
you may fall into a sin.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:26.040
But the reason you fell into the sin is that Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala wants you

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:29.800
to realize how blessed you were when you were not caught in that sin.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.400
Maybe you go through a moment of some slight depression or some anxiety.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.160
But what is a deeper reason?

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:38.200
Or what What is it different a deeper wisdom?

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:46.320
Is that you walk away from that appreciating the moments of ease, of of mental well-being.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.400
And here's what's even more profound.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.800
Our life is always going through ups and downs.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.640
That is the nature of the believer's life.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:59.400
And that's why I quoted the Hadith of the Rasul earlier on.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.920
But here's the deal.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.440
You may be in a dark moment right now.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:06.160
But the truth about life is there's constant change.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:11.280
That's the only uh constant of life is change, quite ironically.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.280
So, when the blessings do return,

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:18.160
now you have a deeper appreciation for them.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:22.640
And so, as scholars have said, they said subhanallah, when you look at it from this

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.440
perspective,

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:29.720
the nikmah, hardship, has now become a ni'mah, a blessing.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.440
So, the idea is we don't want to fall into sin.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:36.680
But when we fall into sin, we have to have the ability to bounce back.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.240
And in order to bounce back, you have to see what was God teaching me through

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:43.240
this. What was I supposed to get out of this?

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.040
And that's what the Imam is teaching us.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:46.680
He says, "Rubbama,

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.200
sometimes,

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.919
darkness will come over the heart.

00:04:50.919 --> 00:04:55.600
And the reason that that may be coming is so that you can gain a deeper

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.360
appreciation

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:02.040
for the blessings that he has been constantly giving you before this hardship.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.160
And here's where it's so profound.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:07.560
The blessings that will come after this hardship.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:12.919
Our job is to become people that don't lose hope when the hardship comes.

00:05:12.919 --> 00:05:14.480
That we don't feel hopeless.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.080
We don't feel forsaken.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:22.120
But we realize that there's a blessing in every situation that we have gone through.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:26.360
So, if you're going through a hardship right now, struggling with a sin, struggling to get

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.840
back on your deen, maybe it's a family difficulty,

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.160
remember that this allows you to become someone of appreciation

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.560
and recognition.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.440
Now, last thing I'll say before we end today's session,

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.080
there's no greater blessing

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.760
than to be someone who recognizes the blessings that they have.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:51.200
That is the greatest blessing because to be a grateful person, shaqir,

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.480
you first have to recognize the blessings.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.600
And if we look throughout the entire Quoran, and if we look at the entire Sunnah

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.200
of the Rasul, why did he do what he did?

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.560
Why did he spend nights in prayer?

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.360
He said one reason.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:12.080
Li akuna abdan shaqura, so that I can become a person of gratitude.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.520
Everything we're doing in this month of Ramadan is based in gratitude.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.960
And there's no way to be grateful unless you value the blessings you have.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.800
And sometimes you only value

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.760
the light because of the dark.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:31.880
May Allah bless you in your moments and bring you light, contentment, and blessings in this

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:34.040
blessed month of Ramadan.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.280
Salam alaykum wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuh.
